title: 'fix(txpool): handle AlreadyImported race in submit_and_watch'
doc:
- audience: Todo
  description: "# Description\n\nFixes a race condition in the fork-aware transaction\
    \ pool where `submit_and_watch` can spuriously return `AlreadyImported` (RPC error\
    \ 1013) even though only a single submission was made.\n\n### The race\n\n`submit_and_watch_inner()`\
    \ performs two steps:\n1. `mempool.push_watched()` \u2014 inserts the tx into\
    \ the shared mempool\n2. `view_store.submit_and_watch()` \u2014 submits the tx\
    \ to active view(s)\n\nBetween steps 1 and 2, a concurrent `maintain()` call can\
    \ run `update_view_with_mempool()`, which imports the tx from mempool into a newly-built\
    \ view. When step 2 then tries to submit to that same view, the view's `ValidatedPool`\
    \ returns `AlreadyImported`.\n\n### Consequences without the fix\n\n- The tx IS\
    \ in the view (imported by `maintain` from mempool), but the RPC caller gets error\
    \ 1013\n- The external watcher stream is never connected to the multi-view listener\n\
    - Critically, `submit_and_watch_inner` removes the tx from mempool on the error\
    \ path (L762), so the tx won't be re-imported into future views if the current\
    \ one is retracted (e.g. due to a fork). The tx's persistence in the pool depends\
    \ solely on the single view that happened to import it during the race\n\nThe\
    \ race window is widened in production by slow `clone_view` operations (1-2s observed).\n\
    \n## Integration\n\nNo integration changes required. This is a bug fix in internal\
    \ transaction pool logic. The fix only changes error handling in `ViewStore::submit_and_watch()`\
    \ \u2014 when no active view accepts the tx and the resulting error is `AlreadyImported`,\
    \ it is treated as success instead of propagating the error. No API changes.\n\
    \n## Review Notes\n\nThe fix is in `substrate/client/transaction-pool/src/fork_aware_txpool/view_store.rs`,\
    \ in the `submit_and_watch()` method.\n\n`submit_and_watch` submits to all active\
    \ views in parallel, then uses `find_or_first(Result::is_ok)` to pick the first\
    \ `Ok`, or the first `Err` if none succeeded. The `Some(Err(...))` branch now\
    \ uses `into_pool_error()` to check if the error is `AlreadyImported`. If so,\
    \ it returns `Ok` with the already-created external watcher, since the tx is already\
    \ in the pool (imported by maintain). Other errors are propagated as before.\n\
    \nTwo tests are added:\n- **Deterministic unit test** (`view_store::tests`): Pre-populates\
    \ a view with a tx, then calls `submit_and_watch` for the same tx \u2014 verifies\
    \ it returns `Ok`. Confirmed this test fails when the fix is reverted.\n- **Concurrent\
    \ integration test** (`fatp.rs`): Races `submit_and_watch` against `maintain`\
    \ across 50 iterations \u2014 verifies `submit_and_watch` always returns `Ok`.\n\
    \n# Checklist\n\n- [x] My PR includes a detailed description as outlined in the\
    \ \"Description\" and its two subsections above.\n- [x] My PR follows the labeling\
    \ requirements of this project (at minimum one label for `T` required)\n- [x]\
    \ I have made corresponding changes to the documentation (if applicable)\n- [x]\
    \ I have added tests that prove my fix is effective or that my feature works\n\
    \n\n## Bot Commands\n\nYou can use the following bot commands in comments to help\
    \ manage your PR:\n\n**Labeling (Self-service for contributors):**\n* `/cmd label\
    \ T1-FRAME` - Add a single label\n* `/cmd label T1-FRAME R0-no-crate-publish-required`\
    \ - Add multiple labels\n* `/cmd label T6-XCM D2-substantial I5-enhancement` -\
    \ Add multiple labels at once\n* See [label documentation](https://paritytech.github.io/labels/doc_polkadot-sdk.html)\
    \ for all available labels\n\n**Other useful commands:**\n* `/cmd fmt` - Format\
    \ code (cargo +nightly fmt and taplo)\n* `/cmd prdoc` - Generate PR documentation\n\
    * `/cmd bench` - Run benchmarks\n* `/cmd update-ui` - Update UI tests\n* `/cmd\
    \ --help` - Show help for all available commands\n\nYou can remove the \"Checklist\"\
    \ section once all have been checked. Thank you for your contribution!"
crates:
- name: sc-transaction-pool
  bump: major
